      <activity id="1727080f-26d1-510e-b715-1294e8d72c41" activityNameId="074bc035-cb7b-5da2-9b11-16559636389b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, at cogen 300kWth, pellets, allocation exergy</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, at cogen 300kWth, pellets, allocation exergy
Inventory for 1 MJ heat from pellets, burned in a cogeneration unit with a capacity of 300 kWth. The multioutput process "pellets, burned in cogen 300kWth delivers the coproducts "heat, at cogen 300kWth, pellets, allocation exergy" and "electricity, at cogen 300kWth, pellets, allocation exergy". The energy efficiency is 30% for electricity and 54% for heat. The exergy factor is 1 for ectricity and 0.164 for heat. This leads to the allocation factor of 0.77 for electricity an 0.23 for heat.
Included are the pellets burning in a 300 kWth cogen unit which in turn includes fuel input, infrastructure (boiler), air and water emissions and electrictiy needed for operation. The efficiency and allocation according to exergy is considered
Location: Data apply to the combustion in Switzerland. 
Technology: efficiency of average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: none
Sampling: Data from literature
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8a8d5d47-a812-3dd6-9e23-0c2088dbbbd8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
